WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.778
"The need for a population of strategies is rooted
in game theory: in a purely cyclic

00:00:04.858 --> 00:00:08.378
game like rock-paper-scissors a single strategy is
meaningless,

00:00:08.458 --> 00:00:11.865
since improving against one opponent means losing
to another.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:18.323
Prior frameworks handle this by training policies
one at a time and discarding the shared knowledge between them.

00:00:18.403 --> 00:00:22.895
NeuPL's insight is that these policies overlap
enormously they share perception,

00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:26.781
memory, and motor skills so training them
independently is wasteful.

00:00:26.861 --> 00:00:32.839
If a single model could hold the whole population
and condition its behaviour on which opponents it faces,

00:00:32.919 --> 00:00:37.697
early skills learned against weak opponents would
directly bootstrap the discovery of

00:00:37.777 --> 00:00:39.640
exploiters to much stronger ones."
